# Large snapshots and generated artefacts - not on origin.
# data/from_validation/ holds ~560 MB of derived .rds copied from
# myc_human_validation. It is REGENERABLE by re-copying from that repo at the
# SHA recorded in data/from_validation/README.md - which is why it is ignored
# and the README is not.
data/from_validation/*
!data/from_validation/README.md

# data/from_myc_mouse/ holds ONE read-only artefact copied from myc_mouse, the
# mitoPPS scores object (511 KB). Ignored to match data/from_validation/'s
# convention rather than because of its size; it is REGENERABLE by re-copying
# from the source path in data/from_myc_mouse/README.md, which also carries the
# md5 and a one-line reproduction check. The README is not ignored.
data/from_myc_mouse/*
!data/from_myc_mouse/README.md

# data/raw/gdsc holds the GDSC release 8.5 drug-response files and the Cell
# Model Passports annotation used by the BH3-mimetic analysis (E31) - about
# 63 MB, plus 72 MB unzipped. Ignored to match data/raw/depmap. E31 and its
# provenance README are on the UNMERGED branch bh3-mimetic-oxphos, not on main;
# the README carries the curl commands, byte sizes and SHA-256 of every file:
#   git show origin/bh3-mimetic-oxphos:data/raw/gdsc_README.md
data/raw/gdsc
!data/raw/gdsc_README.md

# data/raw/depmap is a SYMLINK into myc_human_validation/data/raw/depmap.
# Ignored because git would otherwise track it as a link object that resolves
# only on this machine, and because the ~1.2 GB it points at is gitignored
# there too. The README is tracked and is the only record this repo has of it.
data/raw/depmap
!data/raw/depmap_README.md

# data/menegollo_biclusters/ is TRACKED - its six pinned snapshot files are in
# git and must stay there. These two are the exception and are named one by one
# rather than with a directory rule, precisely so the six keep being tracked.
# They are the METABRIC identifier inputs G3 went looking for (1.07 GB together),
# copied in by the author on 2026-10-02 from outside the pinned snapshot. Their
# sizes, md5s and sources are in that directory's README, section "Addendum".
# NOTE: the `.RData` line further down is a literal filename, not a glob, so it
# does NOT cover these - without these two lines a `git add -A` stages 1.07 GB.
data/menegollo_biclusters/METABRIC_starting_data_final_corr_groups.Rdata
data/menegollo_biclusters/METABRIC_DATA.RData

results/*
!results/.gitkeep
outputs/*
!outputs/.gitkeep

.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj
.DS_Store

# Stray device output from headless Rscript runs
Rplots.pdf

# Claude Code conversation exports (`/export`), which land in the repo root as
# YYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS-<slug>.txt. They are session transcripts, not repo content:
# whatever they record that matters belongs in a dated note under docs/. The
# pattern is anchored to the root with a leading slash so it cannot catch a .txt
# data file deeper in the tree - there are none tracked today, and this keeps it
# that way by accident rather than by vigilance.
/20??-??-??-??????-*.txt
